O|
N|               It is standing in the roadway outside Dora's house.
O|
N,G|               WE SEE it through the finder of a small cine-camera.
O|
S|               EXT. STREETS BY DORA'S HOUSE - DAY
O|
N|               A crowd has gathered outside the house - and we are watching 
N|               them from a corner of the street (ALWAYS THROUGH THE FINDER-
N|               MATTE).
O|
N,G|               WE SEE several Policemen holding back the crowd as two 
N|               Ambulance Men hurry into the house, carrying an empty 
N|               stretcher.
O|
N|               Gentle, whirring sound is overlaid.
O|
N,G|               WE SEE children staring curiously into the empty ambulance - 
N|               and a group of Women talking excitedly to a Reporter.
O|
N,G|               CLOSE SHOT of a SMALL MAN looking at us curiously as he 
N|               approaches (FILLING THE SCREEN WITHIN THE MATTE).
O|
C|                                     SMALL MAN
U|                         What paper are you from?
O|
N|               The finder is lowered.
O|
N,G|               CLOSE SHOT of a Young Man (MARK) sighting a cine-camera. 
O|
N|               He lowers the camera - and turns politely to his 
N|               interrogator.
O|
N|               He seems to have slight difficulty informing his words.
O|
C|                                     MARK
U|                         I beg your pardon?
O|
C|                                     SMALL MAN
U|                         What paper are you from?
O|
N|               Mark smiles at him pleasantly.
O|
C|                                     MARK
U|                         The Observer.
O|
N|               The Ambulance Men come out of the house carrying the 
N|               stretcher... there is a body on it covered by a sheet.  
N|               Mark raises his cine-camera and photographs them. He 
N|               photographs the ambulance as it drives off. He photographs 
N|               the Policemen dispersing the crowd. He photographs his 
N|               Interrogator, who gladly poses for him.
O|
N|               Then he slings his camera over his shoulder, and strolls 
N|               away.
