S|               EXT. A NEWSAGENT'S SHOP - DAY
O|
N|               Mark is staring at a newspaper in the window of a small 
N|               newsagent's shop.  
O|
N|               He glances distastefully at an array of film magazines - 
N|               showing actresses showing everything - then hurries into 
N|               the shop.
O|
S|               INT. NEWSAGENT'S SHOP - DAY
O|
N|               A plump, bald-headed Man stares at Mark.
O|
C|                                     MR. PETERS
U|                         You're late!
O|
C|                                     MARK
U|                         Sorry, sir.
O|
N|               He turns towards a small door at the end of the shop.
O|
C|                                     MR. PETERS
P|                              (quietly)
U|                         Hold on, Mark.
O|
N|               Mark turns round.
O|
N|               Mr. Peters hesitates, drumming his fingers on the counter.  
O|
N,G|               CLOSE SHOT of Mark. He starts to drum his fingers on a 
N|               shelf.
O|
C|                                     MR. PETERS
U|                         Mark... I've a question for you.
O|
N|               He stops drumming his fingers. So, at that moment, does 
N|               Mark.
O|
